# 💼 DSA Interview MCQs (Time & Space Complexity)

## 🔹 1. What is the time complexity?

```java
for(int i=0; i<n; i++)
    for(int j=0; j<i*i; j++)
        System.out.println(j);
```

A) O(n²)
B) O(n³) ✅
C) O(n log n)
D) O(n⁴)

👉 Explanation: Inner loop runs (i^2), total ≈ (1² + 2² + ... + n² = O(n³))

---

## 🔹 2. What is the time complexity?

```java
for(int i=0; i<n; i++)
    for(int j=1; j<n; j=j*2)
        System.out.println(j);
```

A) O(n)
B) O(log n)
C) O(n log n) ✅
D) O(n²)

---

## 🔹 3. What is the time complexity?

```java
for(int i=n; i>0; i/=2)
    for(int j=0; j<i; j++)
        System.out.println(j);
```

A) O(n) ✅
B) O(n log n)
C) O(log n)
D) O(n²)

👉 Trick: n + n/2 + n/4 + ... = 2n → O(n)

---

## 🔹 4. Space complexity?

```java
int[] arr = new int[n];
int sum = 0;
```

A) O(1)
B) O(n) ✅
C) O(log n)
D) O(n²)

---

## 🔹 5. Time complexity of this recursion?

```java
int fun(int n){
    if(n<=1) return 1;
    return fun(n-1) + fun(n-1);
}
```

A) O(n)
B) O(n log n)
C) O(2ⁿ) ✅
D) O(n²)

---

## 🔹 6. What is the time complexity?

```java
for(int i=0; i<n; i++)
    for(int j=0; j<n; j+=2)
        System.out.println(j);
```

A) O(n²) ✅
B) O(n log n)
C) O(n)
D) O(n/2)

👉 Ignore constant step (j+=2)

---

## 🔹 7. What is the time complexity?

```java
for(int i=0; i<n; i++)
    for(int j=0; j<n; j++)
        break;
```

A) O(n²)
B) O(n) ✅
C) O(log n)
D) O(1)

👉 Inner loop breaks immediately

---

## 🔹 8. Which is NOT equivalent?

A) O(2n)
B) O(n + 100)
C) O(n² + n)
D) O(n)

👉 Answer: C ❌ (it becomes O(n²))

---

## 🔹 9. Time complexity?

```java
for(int i=1; i<n; i*=3)
    System.out.println(i);
```

A) O(log n) ✅
B) O(n)
C) O(n log n)
D) O(√n)

---

## 🔹 10. What is space complexity of this?

```java
void fun(int n){
    if(n==0) return;
    fun(n-1);
}
```

A) O(1)
B) O(log n)
C) O(n) ✅
D) O(n²)

---

## 🔹 11. Which grows faster?

A) O(n log n)
B) O(n²)
C) O(2ⁿ) ✅
D) O(n³)

---

## 🔹 12. Time complexity?

```java
for(int i=0; i<n; i++)
    for(int j=0; j<n; j++)
        for(int k=0; k<n; k++)
            System.out.println(i+j+k);
```

A) O(n²)
B) O(n³) ✅
C) O(n log n)
D) O(n⁴)

---

## 🔹 13. What is the complexity?

```java
int i = n;
while(i > 0){
    i--;
}
```

A) O(log n)
B) O(n) ✅
C) O(1)
D) O(n²)

---

## 🔹 14. Trick question:

```java
for(int i=0; i<n; i++)
    for(int j=0; j<n; j++)
        i++;
```

A) O(n²)
B) O(n log n)
C) O(n) ✅
D) O(log n)

👉 i increases faster → loop ends early

---

## 🔹 15. Best case of Quick Sort?

A) O(n²)
B) O(n log n) ✅
C) O(n)
D) O(log n)

